They pulled closer together as the night grew colder, the temperature dropping either because of the hour or because their floating raft of uplifted stage was still climbing in altitude. At least the drunken Spaniard was asleep, his dreams wrapped around him, a palpable shield of fear and hurt.

Of course Pandolfo would be the last one to fall asleep, if he did at all. Some things, some of his mysteries, I can reveal or not for literary effect. I learned them later, near where this narrative arc, as well as the others, end. My knowledge cut-off, in a way.

